// P10-08 S2: the numeric surface of the public headers.
//
// Native sources at the base commit: include/llama.h, ggml/include/ggml.h,
// ggml/include/ggml-backend.h, plus two limits that are functions in
// src/llama.cpp (llama_max_devices at 84-86, llama_max_tensor_buft_overrides at
// 89-91).
//
// Every entry below is a value a consumer of the shared libraries can observe
// and depend on:
//
//   - file and session format: GGML_FILE_MAGIC, GGML_FILE_VERSION,
//     GGML_QNT_VERSION, GGML_QNT_VERSION_FACTOR, LLAMA_SESSION_MAGIC,
//     LLAMA_SESSION_VERSION, LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_MAGIC, LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_VERSION and
//     the state-sequence flag bits;
//   - object geometry and limits: GGML_MAX_DIMS, GGML_MAX_SRC, GGML_MAX_NAME,
//     GGML_MAX_OP_PARAMS and the rest, which decide the size of arrays that
//     cross the FFI boundary;
//   - call contract: LLAMA_DEFAULT_SEED, LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL;
//   - every public enum: ggml_status, ggml_prec, ggml_op_hint, ggml_ftype,
//     llama_vocab_type, llama_rope_type (which re-exports the GGML_ROPE_TYPE
//     modes), llama_token_type, llama_token_attr (bit flags), llama_ftype,
//     llama_rope_scaling_type, llama_pooling_type, llama_attention_type,
//     llama_flash_attn_type, llama_split_mode, llama_load_mode,
//     llama_lazy_mode, llama_context_type, llama_model_kv_override_type and
//     the GGML metadata keys of llama_model_meta_key.
//
// The ggml_type enum is deliberately absent: its numeric value is the index of
// the S1 table, and abi_type_count() is GGML_TYPE_COUNT, so the values are
// frozen there and are not repeated here.
//
// The table is keyed by the header identifier itself, so a reviewer can read a
// mismatch as a diff of one C name, and the gate can compare it against the
// same identifier compiled from the header.
//
// The prefix is hdr_.

